WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:02.177
- De Novo Coronavirus has a new name,

00:00:02.177 --> 00:00:04.940
and there's a ton of new
misinformation out there.

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.940
We're gonna stay alert and not anxious,

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.691
on this week's Wednesday check out.

00:00:08.691 --> 00:00:11.274
(upbeat music)

00:00:13.925 --> 00:00:16.650
The day Today is February 18th 2020.

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:17.760
I need you to know that

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.740
because all the information
I'm about to give you

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.880
is relevant up until this date.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:23.160
Things change really quickly,

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:25.910
especially when it comes
to new viruses like this.

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:28.580
Let's kick it off by
talking about the new name

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:32.310
of the De Novo coronavirus, COVID-19.

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:35.630
CO from Corona, VI from
virus, D for disease

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:39.230
19 'cause it actually
started in December 2019.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:41.050
Actually was a World Health Organization

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:43.177
that decided to give
the De Novo Coronavirus

00:00:43.177 --> 00:00:46.728
the COVID-19 title and they
worked really hard on this

00:00:46.728 --> 00:00:48.890
because they wanted to avoid

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:50.868
a few really important setbacks.

00:00:50.868 --> 00:00:53.960
Number one, they didn't
wanna include the location

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:56.350
'cause it comes with
a lot of stereotyping.

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:59.040
People we're calling this
the Chinese Coronavirus,

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.900
the Wuhan Coronavirus, that's
now what we're calling it.

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:04.550
They wanted to avoid
implicating any animal in this

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:08.450
because as we've seen with the H1N1 virus,

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:10.620
people started referring to as swine flu,

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.300
other ones as the bird flu.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.940
This has nothing to do with animals.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.840
Yes, it started in an animal vector,

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.160
but now it's within humans,

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.800
there's no need to get animals involved.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:21.544
The International Committee
on Taxonomy of Viruses

00:01:21.544 --> 00:01:25.667
started saying that maybe
we should call it SARS-COV-2

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:28.557
but the WHO was like "No don't.

00:01:28.557 --> 00:01:30.577
"Even though it's
somewhat related to SARS,

00:01:30.577 --> 00:01:32.407
"don't put SARS in the title,

00:01:32.407 --> 00:01:34.680
"that's only gonna scare
people", and I agree with them.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.900
COVID-19, that's where I stand

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:38.570
I think that's the best title for it.

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:40.447
Now let's get to the updated numbers.

00:01:40.447 --> 00:01:45.266
Currently, we have
73,000 cases of COVID-19

00:01:45.266 --> 00:01:50.241
with 1.9 thousand deaths
as a result of this virus.

00:01:50.241 --> 00:01:54.330
Now that being said, there was
a huge spike in the numbers

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:56.640
of those who were
infected as well as deaths

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:58.094
last week on Thursday.

00:01:58.094 --> 00:02:00.060
A lot of people started to panic.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:02.940
They started to think that
the virus was worsening,

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:04.977
and it's in intensity and it's spread.

00:02:04.977 --> 00:02:06.770
And that was not happening.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:09.416
What changed and why this
number went up so drastically

00:02:09.416 --> 00:02:11.200
from one day to the next,

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:13.820
was because in the center of
where all this is happening,

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:17.150
the Hubei province where
Wuhan China is located,

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:20.340
they change their way of
identifying who has the virus.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.585
They were simply running
low on testing kits.

00:02:22.585 --> 00:02:24.810
So they decided to do something smart,

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:28.720
those who showed clinical
symptoms of COVID-19

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:32.110
and were exposed to COVID-19,
were diagnosed with it.

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:34.980
That's pretty much what I do
in my office with the flu.

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:36.650
That's called a clinical diagnosis.

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:39.100
If you see someone with a
cough, shortness of breath,

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:43.160
fever and exposure to the
COVID-19 virus, they have it.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:45.680
You don't need to do a kit in that area.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:47.470
This doesn't apply to
the rest of the world.,

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:50.060
but in Hubei Province,
it makes a lot of sense.

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:52.330
So yes, we saw the
number drastically go up.

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:53.650
But there was no need to panic

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:55.630
'cause we had an explanation why.

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:58.710
In fact, the New York Times
just put out a great article

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:02.090
explaining of why we're looking
at these numbers all wrong.

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:03.980
We should not be looking at these numbers

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:05.651
hour by hour, day by day.

00:03:05.651 --> 00:03:08.370
In fact, there's websites
that are dedicated

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:09.920
to tracking this and showing you

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:12.190
where new cases are popping up.

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:14.710
It's almost like they're
gamifying the system.

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:16.150
We don't need to do that.

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:18.100
There's gonna be spikes in how we count,

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:20.220
there's gonna be mistakes in how we count.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:22.787
There's a reason why I'm
giving these updated numbers

00:03:22.787 --> 00:03:25.120
about every week or two.

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:27.397
Because otherwise it gets
too confusing to track.

00:03:27.397 --> 00:03:31.210
If the WHO or CDC needs us
to be alerted of something

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:32.520
they'll let us know.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:35.300
Otherwise, let those other websites panic,

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:37.053
you stay alert, not anxious.

00:03:37.053 --> 00:03:38.670
There's been a lot of talk

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:40.870
about that lethality or death rate

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:43.040
when it comes to the COVID-19 virus.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:44.560
Let's talk about what that means.

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:46.561
When someone becomes ill with any virus,

00:03:46.561 --> 00:03:50.190
there's a specific rate of
those who have a mild illness,

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:53.220
moderate to severe or
critical one leading to death.

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:55.330
When we look at the numbers currently

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:58.950
for this COVID-19 virus,
what we see is that 81%,

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:02.320
which is by far the huge
majority, are mild cases.

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:04.920
14% are moderate to severe, meaning that

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:07.800
the patient will get a bacterial
infection on top of it,

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:10.940
and pneumonia so on, and
then 5% are critical cases

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:13.260
where those people need
respiratory support

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:14.460
or even lead to death.

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:15.600
What does all of that mean?

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.320
In order to understand the impact

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:18.560
that a virus has on a community

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:20.100
we look at a couple of measures.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:21.950
We look at how infective a virus is

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:24.450
meaning how likely is it to
spread within the community,

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:26.490
as well as its lethality rate.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:29.410
Now one of the most deadly
infections out there is Ebola.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:32.070
It has a 50%, about a 50%,

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:35.240
'cause we've seen variations
in this, 50% death rate.

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:39.300
Then MERS, which is the outbreak
that happened in 2012, 30%.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.827
SARS 10%.

00:04:40.827 --> 00:04:44.730
For this virus we're seeing
around 2% fatality rate.

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:47.145
And I wouldn't be surprised
if that number goes down

00:04:47.145 --> 00:04:50.580
as we find more mild cases
that we haven't diagnosed yet.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:51.810
Also, to put in perspective,

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:54.840
the traditional influenza virus
that we see here in the US,

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:59.000
the seasonal flu is point
one to .2% lethality rate.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.650
You've probably also heard on the news

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:02.470
that there's been several cruise ships

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:04.610
that have been quarantined
to prevent the spread

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:07.360
of the COVID-19 virus
because someone on board

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:08.750
was found to be sick.

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:10.754
This is truly happening,
there's actually some Americans

00:05:10.754 --> 00:05:13.460
that were found on some
of these cruise ships

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:15.520
and were brought back to the United States

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:16.529
and held in quarantine.

00:05:16.529 --> 00:05:18.200
I think this is a great opportunity

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.250
to talk about the difference

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:21.580
between isolation and quarantine.

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:24.260
Isolation is what we do
in a medical facility,

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:26.000
but you could do it technically anywhere

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.973
with someone who's already sick.

00:05:27.973 --> 00:05:30.040
Quarantine is what you do with someone

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:32.630
who's either sick, or you're
not sure if they're sick

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:34.500
and you prevent them from exposing

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.010
themselves to other people.

00:05:36.010 --> 00:05:38.203
You can do a quarantine in a cruise ship,

00:05:38.203 --> 00:05:40.880
in someone's home, in an army base,

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:43.050
as long as they're preventing spread

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:44.650
of anything that they might have,

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:45.940
that's considered a quarantine.

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:48.650
Here's five new updates
on the COVID-19 virus

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:49.640
that I think you should know.

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:51.420
Number one, packages.

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:54.044
There's many people that have
a fear and rightfully so,

00:05:54.044 --> 00:05:56.580
of opening packages that
have come from China

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:58.070
and they worried that they may be infected

00:05:58.070 --> 00:05:59.740
with the COVID-19 virus.

00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:01.950
In looking at the testimony from experts

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:05.493
from the NIH, CDC, WHO, it looks like

00:06:05.493 --> 00:06:07.340
our suspicion at the moment,

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:11.220
is that the virus only survives
on surfaces for a few hours,

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:14.740
much like the SARS and
MERS viruses did as well.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:16.960
They are close cousins of COVID-19.

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:20.112
That being said, if you're
handling any packages from China,

00:06:20.112 --> 00:06:22.760
you should be washing your
hands right afterwards,

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:24.260
just to be safe.

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:26.900
The CDC did go on record and state

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:29.980
that the primary spread
of the COVID-19 virus

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:32.360
is not through surface contamination,

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:34.050
it's through respiratory droplets.

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:35.859
So they seem to agree
with the experts as well,

00:06:35.859 --> 00:06:37.170
that's good to know.

00:06:37.170 --> 00:06:39.110
Two, let's talk treatments,

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:41.930
since this is a virus and we
currently have no treatments

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:44.816
other than supportive care,
like giving people fluids,

00:06:44.816 --> 00:06:47.351
making sure that they
have respiratory support

00:06:47.351 --> 00:06:49.670
or if they get a
bacterial infection on top

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:51.250
we can give antibiotics.

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:54.610
Right now they are 80
trials trying to figure out

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:58.010
which antiviral or
antiretroviral therapies

00:06:58.010 --> 00:07:00.350
would work on COVID-19.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:02.410
In fact, there's a new study
that just kicked off in Japan,

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:06.870
using HIV medications on the
virus to see if that works.

00:07:06.870 --> 00:07:08.980
Look, the huge majority
of these are gonna fail,

00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:11.370
but if we find promise,
even in some of these,

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:13.110
that's gonna make a big
difference in the long run.

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:14.790
Three, vaccines.

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:16.450
Since you know, I'm a big fan of vaccines,

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:19.123
and you should be as well,
especially the flu vaccine,

00:07:19.123 --> 00:07:21.940
WHO recently went on record and said

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:24.630
the COVID-19 vaccine is in the works

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:27.960
and can potentially be
completed 18 months from now.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:29.717
I know that sounds like a long ways away,

00:07:29.717 --> 00:07:32.405
but if the situation is
to continue to worsen,

00:07:32.405 --> 00:07:34.010
it's good to know that we have hope

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:35.840
from a vaccine on the horizon.

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:37.982
In fact, we have some
vaccines available now,

00:07:37.982 --> 00:07:40.412
but they're just going into
the beginning trials now

00:07:40.412 --> 00:07:42.650
we wanna make sure they're safe.

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:45.600
So we do do tests on vaccines
to make sure they're safe

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:47.300
before we give them to the general public.

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:50.296
Four, there is a ton of misinformation

00:07:50.296 --> 00:07:52.170
spreading across the web,

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:54.492
about the origins of the COVID-19 virus.

00:07:54.492 --> 00:07:56.085
There's even US senators,

00:07:56.085 --> 00:07:58.430
they're trying to say
that there's a potential

00:07:58.430 --> 00:08:00.230
for bio-terrorism here.

00:08:00.230 --> 00:08:01.688
There is no evidence of this.

00:08:01.688 --> 00:08:05.040
And all that is doing
is creating more panic

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:06.200
and fear mongering.

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:08.430
We should only take
evidence that we have now

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:11.730
and use that to guide
our further research.

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:14.900
Do not put wild unsubstantiated
conspiracy theories

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:16.780
out there, 'cause it just confuses us

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:19.523
and really gives more ammunition
to trolls on social media

00:08:19.523 --> 00:08:22.223
to create grabbing headlines and visuals

00:08:22.223 --> 00:08:24.810
to really misguide the general public.

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:26.350
The current prevailing theory

00:08:26.350 --> 00:08:28.130
is still the one from my first video

00:08:28.130 --> 00:08:30.510
that this virus began in animals

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:32.039
and jumped to a human source.

00:08:32.039 --> 00:08:34.286
Whether that happened in the Wuhan market,

00:08:34.286 --> 00:08:36.549
whether it happened in a Wuhan lab,

00:08:36.549 --> 00:08:39.540
it doesn't even matter if
it was a bat, a pangolin,

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:42.060
it doesn't matter which
animal we're talking about.

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:44.638
That's still the prevailing
theory and until it's disproved,

00:08:44.638 --> 00:08:47.730
there's no need to start
thinking conspiracy theories.

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:49.817
Five, don't believe in self treatment.

00:08:49.817 --> 00:08:52.434
If you think that you may
have the COVID-19 virus,

00:08:52.434 --> 00:08:55.550
contact a health professional immediately.

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:58.670
The WHO just released a
mega warning about this.

00:08:58.670 --> 00:09:00.350
There's things popping up on Instagram

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:03.186
about vitamin C mega
doses, herbal preparations,

00:09:03.186 --> 00:09:06.315
even smoking as a recommendation for this.

00:09:06.315 --> 00:09:08.690
There is no proof that any of this works

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:10.907
and in fact it can put your
life further in danger.

00:09:10.907 --> 00:09:12.740
Please contact the health professional

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:14.680
if you think you may
have been exposed to this

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:16.090
and are experiencing symptoms.

00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:17.360
And also I want to note

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:19.570
that there's becoming a shortage of masks

00:09:19.570 --> 00:09:23.323
both regular surgical masks
and specialized N95 masks,

00:09:23.323 --> 00:09:26.090
'cause it seems like
everyone is ordering them.

00:09:26.090 --> 00:09:28.030
Leave the equipment to professionals,

00:09:28.030 --> 00:09:29.620
people who truly need it.

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:32.150
In fact, there's been 1700 medical workers

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:34.402
who have been infected
by the COVID-19 virus,

00:09:34.402 --> 00:09:36.677
they're already facing significant risk

00:09:36.677 --> 00:09:38.116
do not make the problem worse

00:09:38.116 --> 00:09:41.380
by having them treat patients
without proper protection.

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:44.510
Don't buy masks for yourself
if you don't need them.

00:09:44.510 --> 00:09:46.340
And the CDC has been firm on this.

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:49.230
Most people, ones that
are healthy and not sick

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:51.020
do not need a mask at this time.

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:53.640
We're gonna keep the
hashtag #ALERTNOTANXIOUS

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:54.730
going for this video.

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:57.080
And if you wanna know
the truth about allergies

00:09:57.080 --> 00:09:58.720
and food sensitivity tests

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:00.770
because that involves
your immune system as well

00:10:00.770 --> 00:10:02.290
click here for that video.

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:04.427
I sat down with a world
renowned allergist,

00:10:04.427 --> 00:10:06.203
and did an interview.

